      "level": 2,
      "content": "2.1 Forests of Karnataka"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Karnataka is home to 5 prominent National Parks: Bandipur, Nagarhole, Bannerghatta, Kudremukh, and Anshi (Kali Tiger Reserve).",
        "The Nilgiri Biosphere Reserve, established in 1986, is India's first biosphere reserve and spans parts of Karnataka, Tamil Nadu, and Kerala.",
        "Official Karnataka State Symbols include the Asian Elephant (Animal), Indian Roller (Bird), Sandalwood (Tree), and Lotus (Flower).",
        "The Western Ghats section in Karnataka represents a global biodiversity hotspot with high levels of endemism in flora and fauna."
      ],
      "id": "gd7kq9z"
    },
